# Fixed 2026-11-23, defect 2679, lane-p255-impl (panel 255's R1, route C):
# A handler of C's, raised synchronously, jumps out through a static buffer
# after the program saved into a `malloc`ed buffer and freed it; a correct C
# program, which prints what it returns.
# Symptom: `--sanitize`: heap-use-after-free at `hero_jmp_fingerprint`, read
# at the handler's jump (Linux arm64, 2026-11-22).
# Cause: the runtime kept a record of every buffer a save filled and read a
# fingerprint of the buffer at the thread's next save point or jump, by
# which time the program had given the buffer back.
# Fix: a jump reads ONE word of the buffer it jumps to, which the C library
# reads next and so lives, and decodes the stack pointer from it with the
# key verified before `main` (route C); no buffer a save filled is read at
# any other moment. Where the key cannot be verified a record is read only
# of memory that provably lives (route A).
extern "fixedbugs-2679-shapes.h"
    function shape_handler_heap() -> i32

function main()
    print("handler_heap: " + shape_handler_heap().to_str())
